From aa9fcf1f130b438e9835dd8bfdff0fd80f6689ed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ekkapot Charoenwanit <ekkapot.c@tggs.kmutnb.ac.th>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 13:58:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] heat and pde: real defaults, real chunking, real checks

heat is rewritten. It ran with a budget of it*215208 bytes -- hundreds of
megabytes for one partition -- printed a column of numbers nobody checked and
returned 0 whatever happened. It now takes nx, nt and a byte budget, defaults
to 40/400/150000 for 112 partitions, and checks its gradient twice: against a
hand-written discrete adjoint, and against central differences, which are
exact here because the misfit is quadratic in the initial profile.

pde no longer needs a scenario file. scenario_3.in is embedded, every argument
is optional, and a file named on the command line still wins. It runs the same
problem under two budgets in one process and asserts the gradients agree: 118
partitions against 2, which is the only reference a Crank-Nicholson price under
a rational local-vol surface can have, and a real one, because chunking changes
the elimination order completely.

Chunking pde found a defect the example itself had. CN was built once outside
the checkpoint loop, so its active arrays outlived a partition boundary and
were read on the next pass, splicing a freed graph node into the new graph --
ASan reports use-after-free in Vertex::kill(). Safe only while the example did
not chunk. The same mistake without arrays does not crash; it silently returns
a zero derivative. Documented at the construction site.

Both are now in RANK_EXAMPLES and SAN_EXAMPLES. Verified at 1,2,3,4,7,8 ranks
and under ASan, all clean. The stale submit.sh batch scripts, which invoked
./main with the old argument order, are removed.

